  "body": "Good day,\r\n\r\nMy package version is 0.34.1.1++1+stretch1\r\n\r\nI recently noticed the following:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ ls -la /etc/matrix-synapse/                                                                                                                            \r\ntotal 52\r\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 matrix-synapse nogroup  4096 Jan 29 19:21 .\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 90 root           root     4096 Jan 28 21:59 ..\r\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 root           root     4096 Dec  4 21:36 conf.d\r\n-rw-r--r--  1 matrix-synapse nogroup    59 Dec  4 21:38 homeserver.signing.key\r\n-rw-r--r--  1 matrix-synapse nogroup  1017 Dec  4 21:38 homeserver.tls.crt\r\n-rw-r--r--  1 matrix-synapse nogroup   466 Dec  4 21:38 homeserver.tls.dh\r\n-rw-r--r--  1 matrix-synapse nogroup  1704 Dec  4 21:38 homeserver.tls.key\r\n-rw-r--r--  1 matrix-synapse nogroup 19657 Jan 28 22:08 homeserver.yaml\r\n-rw-r--r--  1 root           root      672 Jan 28 20:03 log.yaml\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe /etc/matrix-synapse directory itself is world-readable as are some sensitive files under it, like homeserver.yaml and homeserver.*.key.\r\n",
